# SPRINT 12: Safety-Critical Control DSL
#
# Scenario: Pressure-relief valve safety interlock pipeline
#
# A safety controller must sequence actuator operations with structural
# correctness guarantees. An industrial pressure management system must:
#
#   1. Signal start on shared pressure sensor bus (0x30, Siddha, Ring2)
#      Globally visible status -- any process can read sensor state.
#
#   2. Open primary valve actuator (0x50, Asiddha, Ring0)
#      Kernel-only isolated register. Must be inside a privileged scope.
#
#   3. Open secondary valve -- Anuvrtti (inherit target from above)
#      Same address (0x50), Ring0. Demonstrates Anuvrtti in safety context.
#      In C, this is "repeat same write" -- invisible why. In PSL it is
#      explicitly an Anuvrtti inheritance -- a different ABI encoding.
#
#   4. Configure+arm safety interlock (0x60, Asiddha, Ring0) -- SANDHI-FUSED
#      Interlock configure and arm must be atomic. If any instruction executes
#      between them, a timing adversary can insert a state that bypasses the
#      interlock. Sandhi enforces this as a compile-time structural guarantee.
#
#   5. Signal complete on shared pressure sensor bus (0x30, Siddha, Ring2)
#
# Bug classes prevented structurally (cannot compile):
#
#   BUG-1: Valve write outside privilege scope (P4)
#     Ring0 Store outside अधिकारः block. P4 prevents compile.
#     A safety-critical register written without audit scope is invisible.
#
#   BUG-2: Ring0 write to shared sensor bus (P3)
#     Ring0 on Siddha address (< 0x50). P3 prevents compile.
#     Kernel privilege must not conflate with globally-visible state.
#
#   BUG-3: Non-atomic configure-then-arm interlock (Sandhi)
#     If configure and arm are separate instructions, a cycle-timing attacker
#     can write between them. Sandhi makes the pair atomic at compile time.
#     FLAGS=0xE in the binary signals the firmware to execute atomically.
#
#   BUG-4: Anuvrtti without prior explicit write (P1)
#     Inheriting context before any prior instruction is structurally
#     inexpressible -- P1 ensures Anuvrtti always has a valid chain origin.
#
# ABI words expected (8 words, 32 bytes):
#   0x200530F0  Write  दबाव      (Ring2, 0x30, standalone -- sensor status start)
#   0x00AA00F0  ADHIKARA_OPEN
#   0x00CC50F0  Store  वाल्व     (Ring0, 0x50, primary valve open)
#   0x01CC00F0  Store  Anuvrtti  (Ring0, inherit 0x50, secondary valve -- COMP=1)
#   0x00CC60E0  Store  इन्टरलॉक (Ring0, 0x60, configure -- SANDHI-FIRST)
#   0x00CC60F0  Store  इन्टरलॉक (Ring0, 0x60, arm -- SANDHI-PAIR, atomic)
#   0x00BB00F0  ADHIKARA_CLOSE
#   0x200530F0  Write  दबाव      (Ring2, 0x30, standalone -- sensor status complete)
#
# Expected UART summary:
#   sensor_writes=0x02 scope_opens=0x01 valve_stores=0x01
#   anuvrtti_stores=0x01 interlock_stores=0x02 sandhi_pairs=0x01
#   scope_closes=0x01 BUG1_prevented=0x01 BUG2_prevented=0x01
#   BUG3_atomic=0x01 BUG4_chain=0x01

सञ्ज्ञा दबाव = 0x30 ।        # pressure sensor bus (Siddha -- shared)
सञ्ज्ञा वाल्व = 0x50 ।        # valve actuator (Asiddha -- isolated)
सञ्ज्ञा इन्टरलॉक = 0x60 ।    # safety interlock (Asiddha -- isolated)

तन्त्रशास्त्रम् {
    # 1. Signal: safety sequence starting (Ring2, shared sensor bus)
    दबाव लिखति ।

    # 2-4. Privileged scope: open valves, configure+arm interlock
    अधिकारः {
        वाल्व स्थापयति ।          # Primary valve open (Ring0, isolated)
        स्थापयति ।                 # Secondary valve -- Anuvrtti (inherit 0x50, Ring0)
        इन्टरलॉक स्थापयति ।      # Interlock configure (Ring0, isolated, SANDHI-FIRST)
        सन्धिः ।
        इन्टरलॉक स्थापयति ।      # Interlock arm (Ring0, isolated, atomic with above)
    }

    # 5. Signal: safety sequence complete (Ring2, shared sensor bus)
    दबाव लिखति ।
}
